{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AEgiXvtxbZKrdExQwkBS4Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Skill Foundry Portfolio Program â€” Phase-0 Foundation / Crucible Intake\n2\t\n3\t> Status: DRAFT for Crucible Stage-0 intake. Authored 2026-06-19.\n4\t> This is the foundation artifact for a multi-wave program that builds a portfolio\n5\t> of skills into Skill Foundry. It feeds the broad Phase-0 researchPrime run and the\n6\t> overarching Crucible session, which lock the program plan. Per-skill deep dives,\n7\t> Crucibles, and Foreman builds happen wave-by-wave (see the Wave Engine).\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## PROGRAM NORTH STAR\n12\t\n13\tBuild a **deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry** â€” a governed set of\n14\tmodel-agnostic cognitive skills, compositional recipes, and (later) stateful agents â€”\n15\twhere every skill carries a **locked North Star**, **journals its own real-use experience**,\n16\tand is **improved during \"sleep\" sessions without drifting from its designed purpose**.\n17\t\n18\tThe first end-to-end proof is a **vertical slice: reproduce the Gelman ANOVA paper** via a\n19\t`recreate-a-paper` recipe that composes the core cognitive skills.\n20\t\n21\t### Non-goals / out of scope (explicit)\n22\t- **GWL agentic harness + t2rs brains are a SEPARATE PARALLEL TRACK**, not this program.\n23\t  Skills/agents here are model/agent-agnostic; a future GWL/t2rs swap-in is allowed but\n24\t  not assumed.\n25\t- **No new Foundry runtime.** Foundry stays a stateless-skill registry + governance gate.\n26\t  Stateful agents (later phases) run on a model-agnostic runtime and call MCP tools +\n27\t  invoke Foundry skills; they do not require Foundry to \"run\" anything.\n28\t- **Handoff pain is handled pragmatically** (content-contract hardening through real use),\n29\t  not as a separate ground-up rebuild â€” Anchor's v10 plumbing is sound.\n30\t\n31\t---\n32\t\n33\t## 1. The portfolio as 5 archetypes (not a flat backlog)\n34\t\n35\t| Archetype | Items | Shape | Home |\n36\t|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| 0. Substrate | GWL harness + t2rs brain; Anchor handoff contracts | runtime/state | **parallel track** (harness GA) / Anchor |\n38\t| 1. Atomic cognitive skills | Gandalf, Jumper, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, analytic-code, ML-code, doc-writing, legal | stateless, model-tiered personas | Foundry SKILL.md |\n39\t| 2. Compositional recipes | recreate-a-paper, propose-extensions, code-verification | orchestrate archetype 1 via Crucibleâ†’Foreman | Foundry recipe layer |\n40\t| 3. Stateful/integration agents | Ecgberht, calendar/email, Anchor-as-app | persistence, events, MCP | agnostic runtime + Foundry skills |\n41\t| 4. Personal/lifestyle | exercise, YouTube curation, memorization | lightweight stateful loops | agnostic runtime + Foundry skills |\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## 2. The Wave Engine â€” repeating 4-stage cadence\n46\t\n47\tEvery skill/recipe is built by one wave, all waves run the same cadence:\n48\t\n49\t```\n50\t[1] researchPrime DEEP DIVE   best-in-class method + named reference impls + failure modes\n51\t                              for THIS one skill (deep, not broad)\n52\t[2] CRUCIBLE (specific)        North Star = this skill; vetted implementation plan\n53\t[3] FOREMAN                    builds to GREEN against Foundry gates\n54\t[4] REVIEW + TEST + LEARN      critical review (Gandalf); run on 2-3 real tasks;\n55\t                              SEED the skill's journal with first lessons; register in map.json\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tA wave is not \"done\" until its skill has: a locked `NORTH-STAR.md`, a `journal/` with â‰¥1\n59\treal-use entry, a seeded `LESSONS.md`, and GREEN Foundry gates.\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## 3. Per-skill repository structure (the deep skill repo)\n64\t\n65\t```\n66\tSkill Foundry/skills/<skill>/\n67\t  NORTH-STAR.md         # LOCKED designed purpose + non-goals + invariants. Anti-drift anchor.\n68\t  SKILL.md              # the protocol (stateless) â€” includes journaling + improvement protocol\n69\t  references/\n70\t    journal-schema.md   # structured per-project entry format\n71\t    improvement.md      # how a sleep session revises this skill WITHIN its North Star\n72\t  LESSONS.md            # distilled, deduped lessons WITH examples   <-- SHIPS with the skill\n73\t  journal/              # raw per-project entries (stateful; stays home, NOT delivered)\n74\t    INDEX.md            #   rolling index: project -> one-line lesson\n75\t    <date>-<project>.md\n76\t  CHANGELOG.md          # what each sleep-revision changed + why     (stays home)\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\t- **Ships to delivery targets (drift-checked, byte-matched):** `NORTH-STAR.md` + `SKILL.md`\n80\t  + `references/` + `LESSONS.md`. Every invocation carries the locked purpose *and* the\n81\t  distilled hard-won lessons â€” the skill gets smarter at the point of use without forgetting\n82\t  what it is for.\n83\t- **Stays in authoring home only:** `journal/` (raw experience) + `CHANGELOG.md`. They feed\n84\t  improvement; they are not part of the delivered protocol, so they don't trip the drift gate.\n85\t\n86\t### 3a. Per-skill North Star (the anti-drift refinement)\n87\tEach skill's `NORTH-STAR.md` is **locked at build time** and states: the skill's single\n88\tdesigned purpose, its explicit non-goals, and its invariants (what must always remain true).\n89\tIt is the convergence authority for the sleep loop.\n90\t\n91\t### 3b. Lessons-learned journaling\n92\tOn each real use, a structured entry records: the task, what worked, what broke, what the\n93\tskill had to adjust, which tools/strategies it tried (and which failed), and the outcome â€”\n94\twith concrete examples and a one-line summary. Schema is the single source of truth in\n95\t`references/journal-schema.md`.\n96\t\n97\t### 3c. The sleep / improvement loop (North-Star-gated)\n98\tA meta-recipe in the repo: Crucible North-Star = *\"improve skill X from its journal.\"*\n99\t1. Read `journal/` â†’ distill recurring patterns into `LESSONS.md`.\n100\t2. Propose `SKILL.md` edits.\n101\t3. **HARD GATE: every proposed change is checked against `NORTH-STAR.md`. Any change that\n102\t   moves the skill toward a different purpose is REJECTED, not merged.** Drift â‰  improvement.\n103\t4. Foreman applies the surviving edits, bumps `CHANGELOG.md`, and Foundry gates must stay GREEN.\n104\tRun manually now; schedule later. (Spiritual cousin of GWL \"sleep cycles,\" kept local to the\n105\tskill repo since GWL is the parallel track.)\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## 4. Anchor â†” Foundry coordination contract\n110\t\n111\tWhen a skill is used inside an Anchor-orchestrated project (its own worktree), the lessons\n112\tentry is born there and must land in Foundry:\n113\t\n114\t```\n115\tAnchor project run --writes--> project-local journal entry\n116\t        | (Learn stage, end of build)\n117\tCOORDINATION STEP (code lives in the ANCHOR folder)\n118\t        --appends/copies--> Skill Foundry/skills/<skill>/journal/\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\t- **Anchor owns the mechanism** (the coordination code lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`).\n122\t- **Foundry owns the schema + the data home** (single source of truth for the entry format\n123\t  and where journals live).\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## 5. Build roadmap (dependency-honest; Option-B slice as the spine)\n128\t\n129\t| Wave | Skill / recipe | Why this order | Model tier (persona) |\n130\t|---|---|---|---|\n131\t| 0 | Foundation (broad research + Crucible) | defines everything below | â€” |\n132\t| 1 | **Gandalf** â€” critical review | also the Review-stage engine for every later wave | Fable 5 |\n133\t| 2 | **Ramanujan** â€” math/algorithm understanding | paper repro must truly grasp the method | Fable 5 / Opus |\n134\t| 3 | **Literature review** (augmented researchPrime) | grounds the paper in context | Opus |\n135\t| 4 | **Data analysis** â€” find/clean/analyze/report | reproduction needs the data pipeline | Sonnetâ†’Opus |\n136\t| 5 | **Analytic + ML code** â€” R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch | produces the runnable reproduction | Opus |\n137\t| 6 | **Code verification** â€” visual + chunked walkthrough, IDE view | validates faithfulness | Fable 5 (Gandalf-assisted) |\n138\t| 7 | **recreate-a-paper** (composes 1â€“6) | the Option-B slice payoff; forces clean handoff contracts | recipe |\n139\t| 8+ | propose-extensions, Jumper, doc-writing, legal | after the slice proves the pattern | mixed |\n140\t| later | Ecgberht, calendar/email, exercise, YouTube, memorization | agnostic stateful agents (MCP + skills) | agnostic |\n141\t\n142\t**First vertical slice target:** reproduce **Gelman ANOVA**\n143\t(`C:\\dev\\Mathematics Problems\\Partition Mappings\\ANOVA Approach\\Gelman ANOVA.pdf`).\n144\t\n145\t---\n146\t\n147\t## 6. What Phase 0 produces (locked by the broad research + Crucible)\n148\t1. The skill-repo architecture above, validated against best-in-class self-improving-agent patterns.\n149\t2. The journaling schema + the North-Star-gated sleep loop, validated for anti-drift + anti-regression.\n150\t3. The persona/model-tier primitive (how \"persona = method + model tier\" is encoded + routed).\n151\t4. The researchâ†’planâ†’build **content-contract spec** each wave reuses.\n152\t5. The Anchorâ†”Foundry coordination contract (schema + mechanism boundary).\n153\t6. The validated dependency order + the reusable Wave Template.\n154\t\n155\t---\n156\t\n157\t## 7. Persona / model-tier primitive (foundation)\n158\tA persona = a method (the SKILL.md protocol) + a default model tier. Tiers available:\n159\tFable 5 (top â€” Gandalf, Ramanujan, code-verification), Opus 4.8 (heavy reasoning/code),\n160\tSonnet 4.6 (routine/throughput), Haiku 4.5 (cheap pre/post steps). The primitive is encoded\n161\tonce in Foundry and reused across archetype 1, and is the seam where a future GWL/t2rs brain\n162\tcan be swapped in without touching the skill protocols.\n163\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65bfc0f5-4fcf-4ea1-a190-34533ac73310","uuid":"9e4d75ba-855f-42c6-aa70-da64ff5936ed","timestamp":"2026-06-19T22:15:35.725Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\planning\\portfolio-program\\ROADMAP.md","content":"# Skill Foundry Portfolio Program â€” Phase-0 Foundation / Crucible Intake\n\n> Status: DRAFT for Crucible Stage-0 intake. Authored 2026-06-19.\n> This is the foundation artifact for a multi-wave program that builds a portfolio\n> of skills into Skill Foundry. It feeds the broad Phase-0 researchPrime run and the\n> overarching Crucible session, which lock the program plan. Per-skill deep dives,\n> Crucibles, and Foreman builds happen wave-by-wave (see the Wave Engine).\n\n---\n\n## PROGRAM NORTH STAR\n\nBuild a **deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry** â€” a governed set of\nmodel-agnostic cognitive skills, compositional recipes, and (later) stateful agents â€”\nwhere every skill carries a **locked North Star**, **journals its own real-use experience**,\nand is **improved during \"sleep\" sessions without drifting from its designed purpose**.\n\nThe first end-to-end proof is a **vertical slice: reproduce the Gelman ANOVA paper** via a\n`recreate-a-paper` recipe that composes the core cognitive skills.\n\n### Non-goals / out of scope (explicit)\n- **GWL agentic harness + t2rs brains are a SEPARATE PARALLEL TRACK**, not this program.\n  Skills/agents here are model/agent-agnostic; a future GWL/t2rs swap-in is allowed but\n  not assumed.\n- **No new Foundry runtime.** Foundry stays a stateless-skill registry + governance gate.\n  Stateful agents (later phases) run on a model-agnostic runtime and call MCP tools +\n  invoke Foundry skills; they do not require Foundry to \"run\" anything.\n- **Handoff pain is handled pragmatically** (content-contract hardening through real use),\n  not as a separate ground-up rebuild â€” Anchor's v10 plumbing is sound.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The portfolio