uctured per-project entry format\n    improvement.md      # how a sleep session revises this skill WITHIN its North Star\n  LESSONS.md            # distilled, deduped lessons WITH examples   <-- SHIPS with the skill\n  journal/              # raw per-project entries (stateful; stays home, NOT delivered)\n    INDEX.md            #   rolling index: project -> one-line lesson\n    <date>-<project>.md\n  CHANGELOG.md          # what each sleep-revision changed + why     (stays home)\n```\n\n- **Ships to delivery targets (drift-checked, byte-matched):** `NORTH-STAR.md` + `SKILL.md`\n  + `references/` + `LESSONS.md`. Every invocation carries the locked purpose *and* the\n  distilled hard-won lessons â€” the skill gets smarter at the point of use without forgetting\n  what it is for.\n- **Stays in authoring home only:** `journal/` (raw experience) + `CHANGELOG.md`. They feed\n  improvement; they are not part of the delivered protocol, so they don't trip the drift gate.\n\n### 3a. Per-skill North Star (the anti-drift refinement)\nEach skill's `NORTH-STAR.md` is **locked at build time** and states: the skill's single\ndesigned purpose, its explicit non-goals, and its invariants (what must always remain true).\nIt is the convergence authority for the sleep loop.\n\n### 3b. Lessons-learned journaling\nOn each real use, a structured entry records: the task, what worked, what broke, what the\nskill had to adjust, which tools/strategies it tried (and which failed), and the outcome â€”\nwith concrete examples and a one-line summary. Schema is the single source of truth in\n`references/journal-schema.md`.\n\n### 3c. The sleep / improvement loop (North-Star-gated)\nA meta-recipe in the repo: Crucible North-Star = *\"improve skill X from its journal.\"*\n1. Read `journal/` â†’ distill recurring patterns into `LESSONS.md`.\n2. Propose `SKILL.md` edits.\n3. **HARD GATE: every proposed change is checked against `NORTH-STAR.md`. Any change that\n   moves the skill toward a different purpose is REJECTED, not merged.** Drift â‰  improvement.\n4. Foreman applies the surviving edits, bumps `CHANGELOG.md`, and Foundry gates must stay GREEN.\nRun manually now; schedule later. (Spiritual cousin of GWL \"sleep cycles,\" kept local to the\nskill repo since GWL is the parallel track.)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Anchor â†” Foundry coordination contract\n\nWhen a skill is used inside an Anchor-orchestrated project (its own worktree), the lessons\nentry is born there and must land in Foundry:\n\n```\nAnchor project run --writes--> project-local journal entry\n        | (Learn stage, end of build)\nCOORDINATION STEP (code lives in the ANCHOR folder)\n        --appends/copies--> Skill Foundry/skills/<skill>/journal/\n```\n\n- **Anchor owns the mechanism** (the coordination code lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`).\n- **Foundry owns the schema + the data home** (single source of truth for the entry format\n  and where journals live).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Build roadmap (dependency-honest; Option-B slice as the spine)\n\n| Wave | Skill / recipe | Why this order | Model tier (persona) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Foundation (broad research + Crucible) | defines everything below | â€” |\n| 1 | **Gandalf** â€” critical review | also the Review-stage engine for every later wave | Fable 5 |\n| 2 | **Ramanujan** â€” math/algorithm understanding | paper repro must truly grasp the method | Fable 5 / Opus |\n| 3 | **Literature review** (augmented researchPrime) | grounds the paper in context | Opus |\n| 4 | **Data analysis** â€” find/clean/analyze/report | reproduction needs the data pipeline | Sonnetâ†’Opus |\n| 5 | **Analytic + ML code** â€” R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch | produces the runnable reproduction | Opus |\n| 6 | **Code verification** â€” visual + chunked walkthrough, IDE view | validates faithfulness | Fable 5 (Gandalf-assisted) |\n| 7 | **recreate-a-paper** (composes 1â€“6) | the Option-B slice payoff; forces clean handoff contracts | recipe |\n| 8+ | propose-extensions, Jumper, doc-writing, legal | after the slice proves the pattern | mixed |\n| later | Ecgberht, calendar/email, exercise, YouTube, memorization | agnostic stateful agents (MCP + skills) | agnostic |\n\n**First vertical slice target:** reproduce **Gelman ANOVA**\n(`C:\\dev\\Mathematics Problems\\Partition Mappings\\ANOVA Approach\\Gelman ANOVA.pdf`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. What Phase 0 produces (locked by the broad research + Crucible)\n1. The skill-repo architecture above, validated against best-in-class self-improving-agent patterns.\n2. The journaling schema + the North-Star-gated sleep loop, validated for anti-drift + anti-regression.\n3. The persona/model-tier primitive (how \"persona = method + model tier\" is encoded + routed).\n4. The researchâ†’planâ†’build **content-contract spec** each wave reuses.\n5. The Anchorâ†”Foundry coordination contract (schema + mechanism boundary).\n6. The validated dependency order + the reusable Wave Template.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Persona / model-tier primitive (foundation)\nA persona = a method (the SKILL.md protocol) + a default model tier. Tiers available:\nFable 5 (top â€” Gandalf, Ramanujan, code-verification), Opus 4.8 (heavy reasoning/code),\nSonnet 4.6 (routine/throughput), Haiku 4.5 (cheap pre/post steps). The primitive is encoded\nonce in Foundry and reused across archetype 1, and is the seam where a future GWL/t2rs brain\ncan be swapped in without touching the skill protocols.\n","numLines":163,"startLine":1,"totalLines":163}}}
